.TH "KLIN" "1" "11/03/2005" "KoanLogic Srl" "KoanLogic Srl"
.\" disable hyphenation
.nh
.\" disable justification (adjust text to left margin only)
.ad l
.SH "NAME"
klin \- Klin swiss army knife
.SH "SYNOPSIS"
.HP 6
\fBklin\fR [\fB\fIklin_opts\fR\fR] [\fB\-c\ \fR\fB\fIcmd\fR\fR] [\fB\fIcmd_opts\fR\fR] [\fB\fIcmd_args\fR\fR]
.SH "DESCRIPTION"
.PP
\fBklin\fR
performs two different tasks depending on the argument supplied to the
\fB\-c\fR
switch: import a site directory tree into the Klin building environment (i.e. the embedded file system), or translate static and dynamic pages into C files.
.PP
.PP
Both commands are normally run by the CMake build rather than by hand. Pass the site directory when configuring Klin and build:
.sp
.nf
    $ cmake \-S ${KLIN_SRC_DIR} \-B build \-G Ninja \-DKLIN_SITE_DIR=${SITE_BASE_DIR}
    $ cmake \-\-build build
.fi
.sp
The build runs
\fB'klin \-c import'\fR
on the site directory, then
\fB'klin \-c translate'\fR
on each page, and links the result into
\fBklind\fR.
Extra import options (\fB\-e\fR, \fB\-k\fR, \fB\-x\fR, \fB\-z\fR, \fB\-Z\fR) are given with
\fB\-DKLIN_IMPORT_ARGS\fR.
Changed pages are retranslated, and the import is repeated automatically when files are added or removed.
.SH "OPTIONS"
.TP
\-h
Display a brief help and exit.
.TP
\-v
Enable verbose mode.
.TP
\-V
Print klin version and exit.
.SH "COMMANDS"
.SS "Translate:"
.HP 6

\fBklin\fR \fB\-c\ translate\fR \fB\-i\ \fR\fB\fIinfile\fR\fR \fB\-o\ \fR\fB\fIoutfile\fR\fR \fB\-u\ \fR\fB\fIuri\fR\fR [\fB\-E\fR] [\fB\-k\ \fR\fB\fIkeyfile\fR\fR] [\fB\-z\fR]
.PP
Translate the active (i.e. a \fI.klin\fR file) or static page \fIinfile\fR
into C file \fIoutfile\fR. 

The \fB\-u\fR option specifies the \fIuri\fR associated with the translated file. 

The \fB\-E\fR option tells \fBklin\fR to encrypt the file content with the key
enclosed in the supplied \fIkeyfile\fR or in the environment variable
\fBKLIN_CIPHER_KEY\fR using AES\-256 CBC.

The contents of the translated files are compressed based on their MIME type if
the \fB\-z\fR flag is given.

.SS "Import:"
.HP 6

\fBklin\fR \fB\-c\ import\fR [\fB\-b\ \fR\fB\fIuri\fR\fR] [\fB\-e\ \fR\fB\fIpattern\fR\fR] [\fB\-x\ \fR\fB\fIpattern\fR\fR] [\fB\-k\ \fR\fB\fIkeyfile\fR\fR] [\fB\-Z\ \fR\fB\fIpattern\fR\fR] [\fB\-z\fR] \fB\fIdir\fR\fR
.PP
Import the site tree starting at
\fIdir\fR
into the Klin building environment. The command writes
\fIautogen.cmake\fR,
the list of pages and how to translate each one, read by the CMake build, and
\fIregister.c\fR,
the glue by which the translated pages are linked into the HTTP/S server. 

When the \fB\-e\fR flag is given, the files matching the specified
\fIpattern\fR will be encrypted using the key enclosed in the supplied
\fIkeyfile\fR or in the environment variable
\fBKLIN_CIPHER_KEY\fR. 

The user can choose whether to compress all the imported files based on their MIME type, using the \fB\-z\fR flag, or to select a subset matching the supplied shell \fIpattern\fR.

If, while importing, you don't want to include a set of files you can use the 
\fB\-x\fR argument to provide the pattern of files you want to exclude.

Arguments \fB\-x\fR, \fB\-Z\fR and \fB\-e\fR may be used more then once.

.SS "Passwd:"
.HP 6

\fBklin\fR \fB\-c\ passwd\fR [\fB\-r\ \fR\fB\fIrealm\fR\fR] [\fB\-m\fR] [\fB\-n\ \fR\fB\fIiterations\fR\fR] \fB\fIuser\fR\fR
.PP
Read a password from the first line of standard input and print a
\fBuser\fR block for the \fBauth\fR configuration of
\fBklind.conf\fR(5): a salted PBKDF2\-SHA256 hash of the password for Basic
authentication and, for each \fIrealm\fR given with \fB\-r\fR (which may be
used more than once), the SHA\-256 Digest hash. \fB\-m\fR adds MD5 Digest
hashes, \fB\-n\fR sets the PBKDF2 iteration count (default 100000). See
doc/AUTH.

.SH "ENVIRONMENT"
.PP
The following environment variable affects the execution of
\fBklin\fR:
.TP
\fBKLIN_CIPHER_KEY\fR
If set,
\fBklin\fR
tries to read the embedded file system encryption key from it. It is be overridden by the
\fB\-k\fR
option.
.SH "DIAGNOSTICS"
.PP
The
\fBklin\fR
utility exits with
\fBEXIT_SUCCESS\fR
on success, and with
\fBEXIT_FAILURE\fR
if an error occurs.
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.PP
\fBklind\fR(8),
\fBklind.conf\fR(5).
